{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 150 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D13"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the fentanyl citrate shortage on 2012-01-01 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E32", "E29", "E30", "E31"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 1 mL syringes at both Corvale East and Corvale General carry NDC 00641624810 labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc.",
      "cites": ["E3", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 2 mL vials at Corvale General carry NDC 00409909422 labeled by Hospira, Inc.",
      "cites": ["E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) received OAI classifications on 2010-01-19, 2011-06-17, and 2011-08-04, the last being 150 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E10", "E12", "E14", "D13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to Hospira, Inc. on 2010-04-12, 629 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["E19", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. (FEI 2220525) has only VAI inspections in the three years before the posting, with the closest on 2011-04-13, 263 days before.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22", "E23", "D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 74 syringes of 50 ug/mL, 1 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 5.6 to 10 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D17", "D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
